Material copied into this repository

- The goat-transformers Python engine and four of its model modules and
  packs, from https://github.com/USAREUR-AF/goat-transformers at the commit in
  src/open_entity_gateway/_goat_transformers/COMMIT, Apache License 2.0
  (U.S. Federal Government). tools/sync-goat-transformers.py copies them and
  SHA256SUMS lists them.

Material fetched at build or test time, not kept in this repository

- SAPIENT (BSI Flex 335 v2.0) proto files, from
  https://github.com/dstl/SAPIENT-Proto-Files at commit
  244a741c13bcee628f84944aef91e4a66854bd7d. Crown copyright, Apache License 2.0.
  tools/fetch-sapient-proto.py changes their import paths and generates Python
  bindings; the generated files carry the proto files' LICENCE.txt.
- Cursor-on-Target schemas (base event, contact, track) by The MITRE
  Corporation, "Approved for Public Release; Distribution Unlimited", fetched
  by tools/fetch-cot-xsd.py from https://github.com/TAK-Product-Center/atak-civ
  at commit 9f6893dd657feacc35ec5de03dad721c2e44170e for tests only.

Example data

examples/records/ holds records published by first-bite
(https://github.com/USAREUR-AF/first-bite, Apache License 2.0) from its
synthetic weather-station dictionary, and from the synthetic harbour-buoy
dictionary of hello-galaxy-first-bite
(https://github.com/USAREUR-AF/hello-galaxy-first-bite, Apache License 2.0).
tests/vectors/cotify.jsonl holds events written by first-bite's cotify crate.

Optional vendor adapters

vendors/picogrid-ecn depends on Picogrid's ECN SDK (picogrid-ecn-client,
Mozilla Public License 2.0), installed from PyPI. vendors/lattice works with
the Lattice SDK for Python (anduril-lattice-sdk), which is not open source and
is not a dependency: each user installs it separately under the Anduril Lattice
Software Development Kit License Agreement. No file of either SDK is in this
repository, and the Apache License of this repository grants nothing in them.

